{#
    The section bar: a hairline, a tracked-caps label, and an optional
    right-hand item. Used as a section heading on composed pages and as the
    page heading on the list-shaped index pages, which is why the heading
    level is a parameter rather than fixed — a page needs exactly one h1.

    The right-hand item is a link when `linkHref` is given and plain text
    when it is not, so a bar can carry a fact (a count, a date) as easily as
    a destination.

    The arrow is drawn for on-site destinations only. An off-site one already
    carries the external-link icon the global rule hangs off every such
    anchor, and the two marks side by side say the same thing twice. The test
    is the one that rule makes — a "//" in the href — so a bar cannot end up
    with both marks or with neither.
#}
{% macro sectionBar(label, linkLabel = null, linkHref = null, level = 2) %}
<div class="section-bar">
    <h{{ level }} class="section-bar__label">{{ label }}</h{{ level }}>
    {%- if linkHref %}
    <a class="section-bar__link" href="{{ linkHref }}">{{ linkLabel }}{% if "//" not in linkHref %}<span class="section-bar__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>{% endif %}</a>
    {%- elif linkLabel %}
    <span class="section-bar__note">{{ linkLabel }}</span>
    {%- endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
